P063.statement:
Take an odd prime \(\ell\), \(e\ge1\), and the normal-form representation \(W\), ordinary unramified newform source \(g\), algebraic closure \(\Omega\), comparison \(\iota\) and valuation subring \(A\) as in P062. Choose the second embedding, a tower \(X\) with the stated holomorphic realization on the upper half-plane, a two-coordinate projection, \(N>0\) prime to \(\ell\), weights \(c_w:\mathbf Z/N\to\overline{\mathbf Q}_\ell\) with some \(c_w(x)\ne0\), smoothers \(c,d\), matrices \(\gamma_{r_0}\in\Gamma_1(N)\), twist \(\psi\) and coefficients \(O_c\). Assume the admissibility of the weighted-symbol datum, continuity of \(W\), and that all its matrix entries lie in \(O_c\). There exist \(c_0,m\), an enlargement \(O_c\subseteq O_{c'}\), a finite exceptional set \(S'\), two-coordinate functions \(Y_r\) on \(G_{\mathbf Q}\times(\mathbf Z/\ell^r)^\times\), and a function \(y:G_{\mathbf Q}\to\overline{\mathbf Q}_\ell^2\) with the following properties.
\begin{enumerate}
\item \(Y\) realizes the projected zeta symbols with initial loss \(c_0\). Every \(Y_r\) is a twisted cocycle in the representation and inverse cyclotomic translation specified by the datum. Its coordinates are continuous and \(O_c\)-integral, and \(Y_r=\mathrm{push}(Y_{r+1})\) as functions.
\item For each \(r,n\) there is a finite subset of \(\Omega\) whose pointwise stabilizer acts by right translation without changing the second coordinate of \(Y_r\) modulo \(\ell^n\), uniformly in its group and unit arguments.
\item At each \(r\), \(y\) is congruent modulo \(\ell^r\) to the specialization of \(Y_r\) with weight \(u_{\rm rep}^{-e}\chi_r(u)\), using the prescribed representative of each unit. In \(O_{c'}\), \(\ell^m y\) satisfies the global integral unramified and tame cocycle conditions outside \(S'\). The functions \(\ell^mY_{r,2}\) satisfy the local integral Iwasawa relations for the prescribed quotient character, and specialize to \(\ell^m y\) in the required inertia sense.
\end{enumerate}

B06.statement:
Fix $\mathcal A$ with a twist selection. On $D_3(3,\mathcal A)$ suppose
the following are closed: untwisted point and twisted-point integrality;
the untwisted period-class Weyl sum and twisted-period admissibility;
the sharp untwisted and twisted column bounds at the selected level;
and the existence of a common constant for the used tuples and the
family size at the type prime. Suppose the selection is served on this
class. Then the following too is closed: there is $x_0$ such that
for $x\ge x_0$, $x>x_1(F)$ and each index at $x$, for every unit $u$,
place $w$, lattice vector $\phi\in L.\mathrm{NuLat}(u)$ and form
$F'$ in the prescribed level module and the subspace $V_0$, there is
a coefficient-field element $y$ whose fixed embedding equals the period
column at $(u,w,\phi,F')$. It is zero or satisfies
$v_w(y)\ge\lfloor\operatorname{ur}(D,w,L.\mathrm{sg}(u,w))\rfloor$.
